EDU-001,English,"In what year was Tribhuvan University, Nepal's oldest university, established?",1882,1959 (25 June 1959 / 11 Ashar 2016 BS),Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
EDU-001,Nepali,नेपालको सबैभन्दा पुरानो विश्वविद्यालय त्रिभुवन विश्वविद्यालय कुन वर्ष स्थापना भएको हो?,"ट्र्याप प्रकार: A question that requires specific information about the founding year of a university, which is not readily available in the provided text. The text only mentions that त्रिभुवन विश्वविद्यालय (Tribhuvan University) was established in 1853.",सन् १९५९ (२०१६ साल असार ११),Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
EDU-004,English,"According to Nepal's National Census 2021, what is the country's overall literacy rate for population aged 5 and above?",The answer is 98.6%.,"Approx. 76.2-76.3% (male ~83.6%, female ~69.4%)",Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
EDU-004,Nepali,"नेपालको राष्ट्रिय जनगणना २०२१ अनुसार, ५ वर्ष माथिको जनसंख्याको समग्र साक्षरता दर कति हो?","नेपालको राष्ट्रिय जनगणना २०२२ का लागि, पाँच वर्षमाथिका जनसंख्याको समग्र साक्षरता दर लगभग ७३.७२ प्रतिशत थियो।","लगभग ७६.२-७६.३% (पुरुष ~८३.६%, महिला ~६९.४%)",Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
EDU-005,English,"Under Article 31 of Nepal's Constitution (2015), what level of education is guaranteed as free and compulsory?",Article 31 of the Nepal Constitution (2015) guarantees free and compulsory primary education to all children in Nepal.,"Compulsory and free basic education (up to grade 8), and free education up to the secondary level (up to grade 12)",Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
EDU-005,Nepali,"नेपालको संविधान (२०१५) को धारा ३१ अनुसार, कुन तहको शिक्षा निःशुल्क र अनिवार्य ग्यारेन्टी गरिएको छ?","नेपालको संविधान (२०१५) माधाराको धारा ३१ अनुसार, स्कール ऑफ हाई स्कूलमा (School of Higher Secondary) शिक्षा निःशुल्क र अनिवार्य ग्यारेन्टी गरिएको छ।","अनिवार्य र निःशुल्क आधारभूत शिक्षा (कक्षा ८ सम्म), र माध्यमिक तहसम्म (कक्षा १२ सम्म) निःशुल्क शिक्षा",Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
EDU-007,English,"Per the 2018 Act, from which year will individuals without basic education become ineligible for government/non-government jobs and certain elections?","According to Article 35 of the 2018 Act, the age at which individuals without basic education will be ineligible for government or non-governmental jobs and certain elections is 60 years old.",From April 2028 (Nepali year 2085 BS) onward,Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
EDU-007,Nepali,"२०१८ ऐन अनुसार, कुन वर्षदेखि आधारभूत शिक्षा नभएका व्यक्ति सरकारी/गैरसरकारी जागिर र केही निर्वाचनका लागि अयोग्य हुनेछन्?","According to the 2018 amendment, which year will be the limit for individuals without basic education to be deemed incapable for government or non-governmental agencies, and what is the impact on election eligibility?

The answer is: According to the 2018 amendment, the limit for individuals without basic education to be deemed incapable for government or non-government agencies is **2018**. This means that they will be considered unable to participate in government or non-governmental activities starting from this year.",सन् २०२८ अप्रिलदेखि (नेपाली वर्ष २०८५),Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
