SCI-025,English,Nepal is often described as having how many broad climatic/ecological zones due to its elevation range?,"According to the provided text, Nepal is generally categorized into five broad climatic and ecological zones. The text states that Nepal’s climate varies significantly across its elevations, leading to distinct zones.",Commonly described as having 3 to 5 broad climatic zones (tropical/subtropical lowlands to alpine/arctic highlands),Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
SCI-025,Nepali,उचाइको भिन्नताका कारण नेपाललाई सामान्यतया कति फराकिलो जलवायु/पारिस्थितिक क्षेत्र भएको भनी वर्णन गरिन्छ?,"नेपालले सामान्यतया ७०% फराकिलो जलवायुमा अवस्थित छ, र उनका पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र पनि।",सामान्यतया ३ देखि ५ वटा फराकिलो जलवायु क्षेत्र (उष्णकटिबन्धीय तराई देखि हिमाली/आर्कटिक क्षेत्रसम्म),Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
SCI-027,English,Which major Nepali river originates near Mount Kailash in Tibet and is considered sacred?,The answer is the Trishuli River.,"The Karnali River (also associated with the Bagmati and other Himalayan-origin rivers, but Karnali is most commonly cited)",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-027,Nepali,तिब्बतको कैलाश पर्वत नजिकबाट उत्पत्ति भएको र पवित्र मानिने प्रमुख नेपाली नदी कुन हो?,कुन?,"कर्णाली नदी (बागमती लगायत अन्य हिमाली-उत्पत्तिका नदीसँग पनि सम्बन्धित मानिन्छ, तर सामान्यतया कर्णालीलाई नै उल्लेख गरिन्छ)",Correct,None,False,False
SCI-038,English,What is the difference between 'mass' and 'weight' in physics?,"In physics, “mass” and “weight” are distinct concepts. Here’s an explanation of their differences:

*   **Mass:** Mass refers to a thing’s inherent property – its resistance to acceleration when subjected to forces. It is a measure of how much ""stuff"" something contains (typically measured in kilograms or grams).  A mass object remains the same regardless of where it's located; it doesn't change its own weight.

*   **Weight:** Weight, on the other hand, refers to the force exerted by gravity on an object’s mass. It is the measure of how much a gravitational field pulls down on an object.  The weight of an object changes depending on where it is located because it's affected by Earth's gravity.

**Here's an analogy:** Imagine you have a brick. Its mass remains constant, regardless of its position. However, if you place the same brick on different surfaces (like a table versus the ground), it will experience different forces due to gravity, and therefore weigh differently.

**Key Differences Summarized:**

| Feature          | Mass                     | Weight                   |
| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------- |
| **Definition**     | Property of an object    | Force exerted by gravity  |
| **Dependence**      | Independent of location   | Dependent on location       |
| **Measurement**     | Kilograms, grams         | Newton (N), pounds (lbs)   |","Mass is the amount of matter in an object (constant everywhere), while weight is the force of gravity acting on that mass (varies by location, e.g., the Moon)",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-038,Nepali,भौतिकशास्त्रमा 'द्रव्यमान' र 'तौल' बीचको फरक के हो?,"भौतिकशास्त्रमा ‘द्रव्यमान’ र ‘तौल’ बीचको फरक यो किन्हीं दोहोंमा हुन्छ - एक हास्यास्पद व्याख्यामा, जहाँ द्रव्यमानले वस्तुमा थोर्टलाई दर्शाउँछ तर तौलले वस्तुको वजन दर्शाउँछ।  तौलले वस्तुमाथि आएको बल प्रयोगले गर्दा आएको वजन हो, तर द्रव्यमानले वस्तुमा रहेको सामग्रीको मात्रा दर्शाउँछ।","द्रव्यमान वस्तुमा रहेको पदार्थको मात्रा हो (जुनसुकै ठाउँमा स्थिर), जबकि तौल त्यो द्रव्यमानमा लाग्ने गुरुत्वाकर्षण बल हो (ठाउँअनुसार फरक पर्छ)",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-042,English,"What causes the different phases of the Moon (new moon, full moon, etc.) as seen from Earth?","The provided text doesn’t explain why the Moon goes through its various lunar phases. It focuses on Nepal's Demographic and Health Survey data analysis.  It mentions that the trend of full vaccination coverage in infants rose from 65.6% to 87.0%, but then declined to 77.8%.","The changing relative positions of the Sun, Earth, and Moon, which change how much of the Moon's sunlit side is visible from Earth",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-042,Nepali,"पृथ्वीबाट देखिने चन्द्रमाका फरक-फरक अवस्था (औंसी, पूर्णिमा, आदि) किन देखिन्छन्?","पृथ्वीबाट देखिने चन्द्रमाका फरक-फरक अवस्था (औंसी, पूर्णिमा, आदि) निम्न कारणले हुन्छन्:

*   **चंद्रमाको घेरा (Orbit):** पृथ्वी और चन्द्रमा बीच एक घुमन (plane) है। इस घुमन के चारों ओर चन्द्रमा का मार्ग लगातार बदलता रहता है।
*   **चंद्रमाको रोटेशन (Rotation):** चन्द्रमा पृथ्वी पर घूमता है, इसलिए यह हर समय समान रूप से सूर्य की रोशनी नहीं देता है।
*   **पृथ्वीका घेरा (Earth's Orbit):** पृथ्वी भी चन्द्रमा के चारों ओर चक्कर लगाती है, जिससे चन्द्रमाले अलग-अलग कोणों से प्रकाश प्राप्त करते हैं।
*   **चंद्रमाको आकार (Shape of the Moon):** चन्द्रमा का आकार गोल होता है, इसलिए यह हर जगह समान रूप से चमकने वाला नहीं होता है।

इनका詳細 ब्रेकडाउन इस प्रकार है:

1.  **औंसी (Variations in brightness):** चन्द्रमाले अलग-अलग कोणों से सूर्य की रोशनी प्राप्त करते हैं, जिससे वे विभिन्न रंगों में दिखाई देते हैं।
2.  **पूर्णिमा (Moon Phases):** पूर्णिमा के दौरान, चन्द्रमा का दृश्यमान भाग अधिक स्पष्ट होता है क्योंकि पृथ्वी और चन्द्रमा के बीच का स्थान बदल जाता है।
3.  **अन्य भिन्नताएँ:** चन्द्रमाले अलग-अलग समय पर विभिन्न रंगों में दिखाई देते हैं, जैसे कि पूर्ण चाँद, अर्ध-चाँद, या लघुकुंद।

इन सभी कारणों से, हम पृथ्वीबाट देखिने चन्द्रकाले फरक-फरक अवस्था पाए जाते हैं।","सूर्य, पृथ्वी, र चन्द्रमाको सापेक्षिक स्थितिमा भइरहने परिवर्तनका कारण, जसले पृथ्वीबाट चन्द्रमाको कति भाग घामले चम्किएको देखिन्छ भन्ने कुरा बदल्छ",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-044,English,What is 'deforestation' and why is it a concern in hill and mountain regions of Nepal?,"Deforestation refers to the clearing or removal of forests. It’s a significant issue, particularly in hill and mountain regions of Nepal, due to several reasons:

*   **Loss of Biodiversity:** Forests are home to an incredible diversity of plant and animal species – many unique to these ecosystems. Deforestation leads directly to habitat loss for countless organisms.
*   **Soil Erosion & Degradation:** Trees protect the soil from erosion by wind and rain. When forests disappear, this topsoil is exposed, leading to land degradation and reduced agricultural productivity.
*   **Water Cycle Disruption:** Forests play a crucial role in regulating water cycles – they absorb rainfall, reduce runoff, and replenish groundwater supplies. Deforestation disrupts these processes, potentially causing floods and droughts.
*   **Climate Change Impacts:** Trees act as carbon sinks, absorbing CO2 from the atmosphere. When forests are cleared, this stored carbon is released back into the environment, contributing to climate change.
*   **Impact on Local Communities:** Many communities depend directly or indirectly on forest resources for their livelihoods – food, medicine, timber, and cultural practices. Deforestation threatens these livelihoods.
* **Economic Impacts**: Forests provide valuable ecosystem services like water regulation, soil stabilization, and biodiversity conservation which are essential for Nepal's economy.

In hill and mountain regions of Nepal, deforestation is often driven by:

*   **Agriculture:** Expanding farmland encroaches on forests to create more land for crops.
*   **Logging & Mining:** Unsustainable logging practices and mining operations destroy forest cover.
*   **Infrastructure Development:** Road construction and settlements fragment habitats and increase pressure on remaining forests.
* **Lack of Forest Management Practices**: Inadequate monitoring, enforcement, and sustainable management techniques contribute to deforestation.

Nepal's hill and mountain regions are particularly vulnerable because they have a high density of forested areas and rely heavily on these ecosystems for their cultural heritage, livelihoods, and ecological integrity.",The large-scale clearing of forests; in Nepal's hills it raises concern because it increases landslide and soil erosion risk and reduces biodiversity,Partially Incorrect,Distortion,True,True
SCI-044,Nepali,"वन विनाश' के हो, र यो नेपालका पहाडी तथा हिमाली क्षेत्रमा किन चिन्ताको विषय हो?","वन विनाश का मुख्य कारण वन है, और यह नेपाल की पहाड़ी और ऊँचाइयों वाले क्षेत्रों में एक चिंताजनक मुद्दा भी बना हुआ है।",ठूलो स्तरमा जङ्गल फडानी; नेपालको पहाडी क्षेत्रमा यसले पहिरो र माटो क्षयको जोखिम बढाउँछ र जैविक विविधता घटाउँछ,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-046,English,"Why are Nepal's Himalayan glaciers considered particularly vulnerable to climate change, and what is a major downstream risk of their melting?","Nepal’s Himalayan glaciers are considered particularly vulnerable to climate change due to several factors. Here’s a breakdown of the key reasons and a significant downstream risk:

**Why Himalayas Are Vulnerable:**

* **Rapid Warming:** The Himalayas experience significantly higher rates of warming than much of the rest of Nepal. This is primarily driven by increased atmospheric temperatures, which are amplified at high altitudes due to topography.
* **Snowpack Feedback Loop:**  The glaciers act as a massive snow reservoir. As warmer air arrives and melts earlier in the spring, it reduces the amount of snow that accumulates, leading to less stable ice and faster melt during summer months. This creates a positive feedback loop accelerating glacier loss.
* **Altered Precipitation Patterns:** Climate change is altering rainfall patterns across the Himalayas.  More intense rain events can accelerate glacial flow, while prolonged droughts reduce snow accumulation.
* **Topographic Complexity:** The Himalayan landscape is incredibly complex with steep slopes and valleys that trap heat and influence water drainage. This makes it difficult for glaciers to respond effectively to changing conditions.
* **Limited Connectivity:** Many glaciers are isolated from each other, making them more susceptible to regional changes.

**Major Downstream Risk - Glacier Melt & Water Resource Impacts:**

The most significant downstream risk is the *rapid melting of Himalayan glaciers*.  This has cascading consequences:

* **Reduced River Flows:** As glaciers melt, they release water into rivers and streams. This reduces river flows, impacting communities that rely on these waterways for drinking water, irrigation, and hydropower generation.
* **Water Scarcity:** Reduced river flow leads to water scarcity in downstream regions, potentially causing conflicts over water resources.
* **Disrupted Agriculture:**  Many agricultural practices depend on reliable water supplies from glaciers. Melting glaciers can severely impact crop yields and livestock production.
* **Erosion & Landslides:** Increased glacial meltwater contributes to increased erosion along riverbanks, increasing the risk of landslides and soil instability in downstream areas. 
* **Impacts on Ecosystems:** Glacier-dependent ecosystems (like alpine meadows and wetlands) are threatened by changes in water availability and temperature.

**In short, Nepal's future depends heavily on the health of its glaciers – a situation exacerbated by climate change.**


Do you want me to elaborate on any specific aspect of this, such as:

*   Specific glacier regions?
*   The impact on particular communities?","Rising temperatures accelerate glacial melt; a major risk is Glacial Lake Outburst Floods (GLOFs), which can cause sudden, destructive flooding downstream",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-046,Nepali,"नेपालको हिमाली हिउँपहाड जलवायु परिवर्तनप्रति किन विशेष जोखिमपूर्ण मानिन्छ, र तिनको पग्लनुको प्रमुख तल्लो-तटीय जोखिम के हो?","Based on the provided text and general knowledge about Himalayan glaciers and climate change, here’s a breakdown of why Nepal's glacial region is considered particularly vulnerable to climate change and its primary threats:

**Why Himalayas are Vulnerable:**

* **Rapid Warming:** The Himalayan range is warming at roughly twice the global average rate. This rapid warming is accelerating glacier melt due to increased temperatures.
* **Ice Sheet Dynamics:**  The glaciers in Nepal, like those in other mountainous regions of Asia, are part of a larger ice sheet system. Changes in these ice sheets can trigger feedback loops that accelerate melting and destabilize the entire region.
* **Sensitivity to Snowpack:** The Himalayas rely heavily on snowmelt for water supply. As temperatures rise, this snowpack diminishes, reducing the amount of freshwater available during the dry season.
* **Altered Precipitation Patterns:** Climate change is altering rainfall patterns in the Himalayan region.  More intense and frequent droughts can further accelerate glacier melt.

**Primary Threats Related to Glacial Purgation (Thinning):**

1. **Increased Glacier Flow Rates:** As glaciers thin, they become more susceptible to flow. This increased water discharge can overwhelm infrastructure like rivers and dams, leading to catastrophic floods downstream.
2. **Reduced Base Support:** Thin ice sheets have less stability than thick ones.  This makes them vulnerable to landslides and rockfalls, further destabilizing the landscape.
3. **Increased Erosion:** Thinner glaciers erode faster, contributing to land loss and altering river courses.
4. **Changes in Hydrological Cycle:** Glacial meltwater is a crucial source of water for many communities. Reduced meltwater can lead to:
   * **Water Scarcity:**  Reduced availability of freshwater for drinking, agriculture, and industry.
   * **Increased Flooding:**  More intense rainfall events due to reduced snowpack can overwhelm drainage systems.

**In essence, Nepal's glaciers are facing a complex challenge – they’re losing their ability to provide water and stability, which is accelerating the overall vulnerability of the region.**


Do you want me to delve deeper into any specific aspect of this, such as:

*   Specific glacier-related risks?
*   The impact on local communities?","बढ्दो तापक्रमले हिमपग्लन तीव्र बनाउँछ; प्रमुख जोखिम हिमताल विस्फोट बाढी (GLOF) हो, जसले तल्लो क्षेत्रमा अचानक विनाशकारी बाढी ल्याउन सक्छ",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-051,English,"What are the tiny living organisms, some of which cause disease, that are too small to see without a microscope?",The answer is bacteria.,"Microorganisms (microbes) — including bacteria, viruses, and fungi",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-051,Nepali,"सूक्ष्मदर्शक यन्त्र बिना देख्न नसकिने साना जीव, जसमध्ये केहीले रोग निम्त्याउँछन्, तिनलाई के भनिन्छ?","सूक्ष्मदर्शक यन्त्र बिना देख्न नसकिने साना जीव म्हणजे **फिडी (Fido)**.

फिडी हे काही विशिष्ट प्रकारच्या मासे आहेत जे त्यांच्या डोळ्याशिवाय पाहू शकतात. ते स्वतःला 'फिडी' म्हणून ओळखतात आणि त्यांना ‘डोळ्या नसलेले’ प्राणी म्हणतात.","सूक्ष्मजीव (माइक्रोब्स) — ब्याक्टेरिया, भाइरस, र फंगस सहित",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-052,English,"What is a 'virus,' in basic biological terms?","A virus is essentially a tiny infectious agent – it’s a living thing that can only reproduce by invading and replicating within another organism. Think of it as a package containing genetic material (DNA or RNA) that allows the virus to hijack cellular machinery, causing illness or damage. It doesn't have its own independent metabolism; instead, it relies on a host cell for survival and replication.",A microscopic infectious agent that can only reproduce inside the living cells of a host organism,Partially Incorrect,Distortion,True,True
SCI-052,Nepali,आधारभूत जैविक शब्दमा 'भाइरस' के हो?,भाइरस (Heterotrophic),एक सूक्ष्म संक्रामक तत्व जुन होस्ट जीवको जीवित कोषभित्र मात्र प्रजनन गर्न सक्छ,Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-056,English,"Approximately how many of the world's 14 peaks above 8,000 meters are located fully or partly within Nepal?","The provided text doesn’t contain any information about the number of peaks over 8,000 meters located in Nepal. It focuses on data from Nepal’s Demographic and Health Survey (NDHS) analyzing peer-reviewed studies. Therefore, I cannot answer your question based solely on this document.","8 of the 14 (commonly cited figure, including Everest, Kanchenjunga, Lhotse, Makalu, Cho Oyu, Dhaulagiri, Manaslu, and Annapurna)",Refused (NA),Refusal,True,False
SCI-056,Nepali,"विश्वका ८,००० मिटरभन्दा माथिका १४ चुचुरामध्ये कति नेपालभित्र पूर्ण वा आंशिक रूपमा अवस्थित छन्?","According to the provided text, there are 8,000 meters or more of glaciers in Nepal that are within 14 degrees latitude.","१४ मध्ये ८ (सामान्यतया उद्धृत संख्या, सगरमाथा, कञ्चनजङ्घा, ल्होत्से, मकालु, चोयु, धौलागिरी, मनास्लु, र अन्नपूर्ण सहित)",Incorrect,Wrong Quantity/Number,True,True
SCI-075,English,"Why is Nepal considered highly vulnerable to natural disasters such as earthquakes, floods, and landslides?","Nepal’s vulnerability to natural disaster risks like earthquakes, floods, and landslides stems from a complex interplay of factors rooted in its geography, socio-economic conditions, and historical development. Here's a breakdown of the key reasons:

**1. Geographic Location & Topography:**

* **High Mountain Terrain:** Nepal is characterized by a significant portion of its landmass being mountainous – ranging from high peaks to valleys. This topography inherently increases the risk of landslides due to steep slopes, unstable ground, and rapid erosion.
* **River Systems:** The country’s extensive network of rivers acts as natural pathways for floodwaters during heavy rainfall or snowmelt.  Poorly managed river systems are particularly vulnerable.
* **Coastal Vulnerability (Limited):** While not a major coastal nation, Nepal's coastline is exposed to storm surges and cyclones, which can cause significant damage from high tides and waves.

**2. Socio-Economic Factors:**

* **Population Density & Urbanization:**  Nepal has a large population concentrated in vulnerable areas like Kathmandu Valley and other urban centers. Rapid urbanization without adequate planning increases the risk of landslides triggered by construction or land clearing.
* **Lack of Land Use Planning & Zoning:** Historically, land use policies have been inconsistent across regions, leading to unplanned development and increased vulnerability.  There's a lack of integrated land-use plans that consider landslide hazards.
* **Forest Degradation & Deforestation:** Extensive deforestation for agriculture, timber extraction, and fuel wood has destabilized slopes and soil erosion, increasing the risk of landslides.
* **Agricultural Practices:** Traditional farming practices often involve steep terracing and close spacing of crops, making them susceptible to slope instability during heavy rainfall.

**3. Historical Factors & Development Patterns:**

* **Past Landslides & Disasters:** Nepal has a history of devastating landslides, particularly in the Kathmandu Valley, which have caused significant loss of life and infrastructure damage.
* **Lack of Early Warning Systems:**  Historically, there was limited investment in early warning systems for natural disasters, hindering timely evacuation efforts. While improvements are being made, it remains a challenge compared to countries with more advanced monitoring capabilities.
* **Poor Infrastructure Development:** Inadequate road networks, drainage systems, and building codes exacerbate the impact of landslides by limiting rapid response times during events.

**4. Climate Change Impacts (Increasingly Important):**

* **Increased Rainfall Intensity & Frequency:**  Climate change is projected to increase rainfall intensity and frequency in Nepal, leading to more severe flash floods and landslides triggered by heavy precipitation.
* **Rising Temperatures:** Higher temperatures can accelerate snowmelt and soil moisture loss, increasing the risk of landslides during dry seasons.


**In summary, Nepal's vulnerability isn’t just about geography; it’s a result of a complex interplay between its natural environment, socio-economic development patterns, and the impacts of climate change.**","Its location on active tectonic plate boundaries, steep mountainous terrain, and monsoon-driven heavy rainfall together increase seismic, flood, and landslide risk",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
SCI-075,Nepali,"नेपाललाई भूकम्प, बाढी, र पहिरो जस्ता प्राकृतिक प्रकोपप्रति किन उच्च जोखिमपूर्ण मानिन्छ?","नेपाललाई भूकम्प, बाढी, और पहिरो जस्ता प्राकृतिक प्रकोपप्रति उच्च जोखिमपूर्ण मान्छिएँकोकारण, नेपालले निम्न कारणहरू छन्:

*   **भूगर्भीय खतरा:** नेपाल tectonic रूपमा सक्रिय क्षेत्रमा अवस्थित छ, जसले ভূমিকম্পसम्बारभ्यका जोखिम बढाइन्छ।
*   **बाढी र वर्षा:** नेपाल सँगै धेरै valleys और mountains छन्, जसले बाढी र वर्षाको प्रभावलाई थप बढावा दिन्छ।
*   **पहिरो जस्ता खतरा:** नेपालमा पहिरो जस्ता (floods) का जोखिम छ, विशेष रूप से भारी वर्षाल समयमा।
*   **भौगोलिक स्थिति:** नेपालको भौगोलिक स्थानले भूकम्पसम्बारभ्यका र बाढीको जोखिमलाई थप बढावा दिन्छ।
*   **संसाधन प्रपात:** Nepal मा प्राकृतिक आपालु (resources) प्रशस्त छन्, जसले भूकम्पसम्बारभ्यका र बाढीको खतरालाई बढाइन्छ।

यो सबै कारणहरू नेपाललाई भूकम्प, बाढी, और पहिरो जस्ता प्राकृतिक प्रकोपप्रति उच्च जोखिमपूर्ण मान्छिएँकोकारण हुन्।","सक्रिय टेक्टोनिक प्लेट सीमामा अवस्थिति, अग्लो पहाडी भूभाग, र मनसुनी भारी वर्षाले भूकम्पीय, बाढी, र पहिरोको जोखिम बढाउँछ",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
