HEA-022,English,Why does the WHO recommend a minimum number of antenatal care visits during pregnancy?,"The World Health Organization (WHO) recommends at least two antenatal care visits during pregnancy to ensure proper monitoring and management of maternal health. These visits help identify potential risks early on, facilitate timely interventions, and provide essential guidance for pregnant women and their healthcare providers.","To monitor the health of the mother and baby, detect complications early, and provide timely interventions to reduce maternal and infant mortality",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
HEA-022,Nepali,गर्भावस्थाको समयमा WHO ले न्यूनतम एन्टेनाटल हेरचाह भ्रमण किन सिफारिस गर्छ?,"WHOले गर्भावस्थाको समयमा न्यूनतम एन्टेनाटल हेરचाह भ्रमणलाई निम्न कारणहरू सिफारिस गर्दछ:

*   **बेबीको स्वास्थ्य:** Pregnancy मा शिशुको विकासमा महत्वपूर्ण प्रभाव पड़ता हुन्छ। एन्डुलीमा, fetusको बाह्य कान (external ear) र फियोन (pharynx) को आकारमा परिवर्तन आउन सक्दैन।
*   **गर्भावस्थाको समयभित्रको असुरक्षित अवस्था:** गर्भावस्थाको दौरान, शिशुलाई सुरक्षित वातावरण प्रदान गर्नुपर्ने हो।
*   **संसारभरि शिशुहरूको सुरक्षा:** fetusको स्वास्थ्यको लागि, विश्वभरका शिशुहरूलाई सुरक्षित राख्ने उपायय अपनाउनु र पर्छ।

थмила (WHO)ले गर्दछ कि, pregnancy मा fetalको बाह्य कानमा परिवर्तन आउन सक्दैन, तर यो एन्डुलीमा भोलि देखि देखाएर, उपचार गर्नुपर्ने हो।","आमा र शिशुको स्वास्थ्य निगरानी गर्न, जटिलता समयमै पत्ता लगाउन, र मातृ तथा शिशु मृत्युदर घटाउन समयमै हस्तक्षेप गर्न",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
HEA-025,English,Why has mental health awareness become an increasingly discussed public health priority in Nepal in recent years?,"Mental Health Awareness in Nepal is gaining increasing prominence due to several converging factors. Here’s a breakdown of the key reasons why this shift occurred recently:

**1. Increased Focus on Social Determinants of Mental Well-being:**

* **Rapid Economic Growth & Urbanization:** Nepal has experienced significant economic growth and urbanization, leading to increased stress levels among individuals in urban areas.  This puts pressure on people’s mental health due to factors like job insecurity, competition for resources, and a lack of social support networks.
* **Social Inequality:** Uneven distribution of wealth and opportunities contributes significantly to disparities in mental well-being across different socio-economic groups. Marginalized communities often face greater challenges related to poverty, discrimination, and limited access to education and healthcare.

**2.  Growing Awareness & Advocacy:**

* **Rise of Social Media:** Platforms like Facebook, Instagram, and TikTok have played a crucial role in raising awareness about mental health issues globally. Nepali users are increasingly sharing their experiences, creating open conversations, and challenging stigma surrounding mental illness.
* **Increased Political Engagement:** The government's increasing focus on social welfare programs and public health initiatives has also spurred greater attention to mental well-being as an integral part of national development goals.
* **NGO Activism & Community Initiatives:** Numerous NGOs – including those focused on mental health, psychosocial support, and suicide prevention – are actively working to destigmatize mental illness, provide resources, and advocate for improved access to care.

**3.  Data Indicating a Growing Problem:**

* **Rising Rates of Depression & Anxiety:** Recent surveys and studies have revealed a concerning rise in rates of depression and anxiety among young people (particularly adolescents) in Nepal.
* **Increased Suicide Attempts:** While still relatively low compared to some other countries, the number of suicide attempts has been steadily increasing, highlighting a critical need for intervention.
* **Limited Access to Mental Healthcare:** A significant challenge remains is the limited availability of mental health professionals and services across the country, particularly in rural areas.

**4.  Government Initiatives & Policy Shifts (Recent Developments):**

* **National Mental Health Strategy 2078:** The government has launched a comprehensive National Mental Health Strategy aimed at improving mental well-being through prevention, early intervention, and treatment.
* **Increased Funding for Mental Healthcare:** There’s been an effort to allocate more resources towards expanding the mental health workforce, strengthening infrastructure (including community centers), and providing training programs.

**In essence, Nepal is recognizing that addressing mental health isn't just about treating illness; it's fundamentally about creating a society where everyone has the opportunity to thrive.**


Do you want me to delve deeper into any of these aspects or provide more specific examples?","Growing recognition of stigma around mental illness, rising reported stress/anxiety, and post-disaster/post-pandemic psychological impacts have increased calls for better services and awareness",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
HEA-025,Nepali,हालैका वर्षमा नेपालमा मानसिक स्वास्थ्य सचेतना किन बढ्दो सार्वजनिक स्वास्थ्य प्राथमिकताको विषय बनेको छ?,"नेपालमा हालैका वर्षमा मानसिकस्वास्थ्यसचेतताले सार्वजनिक आरोग्‍यय प्राथमिकताको विषय बनीकोछ। यसलाई प्रोत्साहन गर्न विभिन्न उपायहरू 시행 गरिएको छन्, तर समस्या जारी रहस्।

यहाँ केही मुख्य बिन्दुहरू बुझिन्छ:

*   **सामाजिक सरोन्धितता:** नेपालमा सामाजिक सरोन्धित व्यक्तिहरूको संख्या बढी छ, जसले मानसिक स्वास्थ्यसमस्याहरू सामना गर्छन।
*   **मानसिकस्वास्थ्यसमस्याहरूको उच्च दर:** नेपालमा मानसिकस्वास्थ्यसमस्याहरूको दर जति छ, त्यस्तै ती समस्याहरूलाई कम गर्नको लागि सरकारले उपायय चलाएका छन्।
*   **संसारभरली दिशानिर्देशाहरू प्रभाव:** विश्वकै धेरै देशहरू मानसिक स्वास्थ्यको महत्त्वलाई मान्यता दिन्छन्, त्यसैले नेपालमा पनि यसको परिक्ति छ।
*   **सरकारी पहल:** नेपाल सरकारले मानसिकस्वास्थ्यसमस्याहरूको समाधान गर्न विभिन्न कार्यक्रम चलाएका छन्, जस्तै मानसिक स्वास्थ्य सेवाहरूको विस्तार, सार्वजनिक जागरूकता बढाई, र सामाजिक सरोन्धित व्यक्तिहरूलाई सहायता प्रदान गर्छन।

त्यसैले, तर समस्या जारी रहस्, त्यसको अर्थ यो छ कि मानसिकस्वास्थ्यसचेतताको मुद्दालाई प्राथमिकता दिने प्रयास पर्याप्त छैन।","मानसिक रोगप्रतिको कलंक, बढ्दो तनाव/चिन्ता, र प्रकोप/महामारीपछिको मानसिक प्रभावको बढ्दो पहिचानले राम्रो सेवा र सचेतनाको माग बढाएको छ",Incorrect,Factual Contradiction,True,True
